<http://data.silknow.org/object/d8534238-7b40-33b9-94a6-58cf9bac72ca/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Pair of fringes with tassels in green and white silk and yellow cotton. With green horizontal stripe flanked by white ones ribbed vertically by weft shoots. The bundled cotton weft of the braid is bound by green silk warp and decorated with the green and white silk brought over three passes of the weft and under the fourth.\n\nThe tassels are of green and white silk on a wooden rope, and hanging from a cord. Cord attachment holding the tassels are bound into the back at two inch intervals along the braid. The cord is of green silk covering the yellow cotton, and tightly finished and fairly thick. It is continuous, and the tassels hang midway between points of attachments. The tassels of green floss silk over round wooden bead, above wooden truncated cone wound horizontally with white floss silk held down by four double strands of twisted green silk running from apex to base, at which is a bobble of green floss silk."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/d8534238-7b40-33b9-94a6-58cf9bac72ca> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/d8534238-7b40-33b9-94a6-58cf9bac72ca/category/1>
